4,Describing Makasae : a trans-New Guinea language of East Timor,https://researchers.westernsydney.edu.au/en/studentTheses/describing-makasae-a-trans-new-guinea-language-of-east-timor/,"Abstract This thesis constitutes a grammatical analysis of the north-eastern variety of Makasae, a largely undocumented language spoken in the district of Laga in East Timor. With some 110,000 speakers, Makasae is one of four languages in East Timor which belong to the Trans-New Guinea phylum. Although the dialect of Laga is taken as normative in this thesis, variant forms in other dialects ...",Makasae,Trans-New Guinea
