9,Makasai in Timor-Leste people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/13234/TT,"Introduction / History The Makasai people, also known as Makasae or Makassai, are an indigenous group of Papuan origin living in the eastern part of Timor-Leste. They primarily reside in the districts of Baucau and Viqueque, with some presence in surrounding highland and coastal areas. They speak Makasae, a Trans-New Guinea Papuan language distinct from the Austronesian languages common ...",Makasae,Trans-New Guinea
